        "title": "Soil Texture and Structure: Sand/Silt/Clay Triangle, Aggregates",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Soil texture (the permanent ratio of sand, silt, and clay particles) and soil structure (the arrangement of those particles into aggregates) are the two most important physical properties governing water movement, aeration, workability, and productivity. Texture is inherited from parent material and weathering; structure is built by biology and can be destroyed by tillage."
    },
